8). NVL
+++++++

Replaces NULL with a OTHER value

Syntax:
NVL(ARG1, ARG2)

If ARG is NULL → return ARG2
Else → return ARG1


EX1:

SELECT SAL,COMM,SAL+COMM
FROM EMP;(RESULT ALSO NULL)


SELECT SAL,COMM,SAL+NVL(COMM,0)
FROM EMP;(NO NULL)

 2. NVL2
++++++++

Checks NULL and returns 2 different values

Syntax:
NVL2(expr, value_if_not_null, value_if_null)

IF ARG1 NOT NULL → second value
IF ARG NULL → third value


1)DISPLAY THE MESSAGE EMPLOYEES EARNING COMM OR NOT.
EX:

SELECT COMM,NVL2(COMM,'YES EARNING','NOT EARNING')
FROM EMP;


2)DISPLAY TOTAL SAL(SAL+COMM) IF THEY EARN COMM THEN DONT CHANGE THE COMM  ELSE GIVE NEW COMM AS 100.


SELECT SAL,COMM,SAL+NVL2(COMM,COMM,100)
FROM EMP;


